{"parentUuid":"2adc2767-6938-4148-8a58-abcdfa0de504","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017YDRQp4aAxnUhhgaM9rjEe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found the bug. Here's what happened to `6bc86e5832db`:\n\n## What the data shows\n\nIn `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/entire.io`, two commits write this checkpoint to `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main`:\n\n| Commit | Subject | `transcript.jsonl` lines | `checkpoint_transcript_start` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `9659325218` | Checkpoint: 6bc86e5832db | **252** | 237 |\n| `89638c9a22` | Finalize checkpoint: 6bc86e5832db | **17** | 237 |\n\nThe first commit was written at PostCommit time with the **cumulative** compact transcript (252 lines, where the current turn starts at line 237). The second commit — the Stop-time finalize — overwrote it with only the **17-line turn slice** but left `checkpoint_transcript_start: 237` untouched. That's the desync.\n\n## Where the bug is\n\n`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go:2872-2908` — `finalizeInternalCompactTranscript`:\n\n```go\nstartLine := 0\nif readErr == nil && content != nil {\n    startLine = content.Metadata.GetTranscriptStart()  // = 237 from previous metadata\n}\nreturn compactTranscriptForV2(ctx, ag, redactedTranscript, startLine)  // produces scoped delta\n```\n\nThen at `manual_commit_hooks.go:2825` this scoped compact is fed into `updateOpts.CompactTranscript`, which `V2GitStore.updateCommittedMain` (`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go:248-258`) **replaces wholesale** in the tree. Metadata is never rewritten in that path, so `checkpoint_transcript_start: 237` survives.\n\n## Why it should match the PostCommit path\n\nCompare with `buildInternalCompactTranscript` (`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go:558-580`), the version used at PostCommit. It deliberately does the opposite:\n\n```go\nscopedCompact := compactTranscriptForV2(compactCtx, ag, redacted, state.CheckpointTranscriptStart)  // for offset calc only\nfullCompact   := compactTranscriptForV2(compactCtx, ag, redacted, 0)  // <-- this is what gets stored\n...\nreturn compactTranscriptResult{ Transcript: fullCompact, StartLine: startLine }\n```\n\nThe comment on line 569-571 spells out the invariant: \"v2 /main replaces the session's transcript.jsonl on each write, so we must include all prior content, not just the new portion.\" Finalize violates that invariant.\n\nThe post-commit codepath also intentionally leaves metadata's `checkpoint_transcript_start` alone (`manual_commit_hooks.go:2862-2867`) for carry-forward correctness — fine, because in its world the stored transcript is cumulative so the offset is meaningful.\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `finalizeInternalCompactTranscript`, pass `0` (or simply call the same `compactTranscriptForV2(..., 0)` used for `fullCompact` above) so the finalized commit re-stores the cumulative compact. Then `checkpoint_transcript_start: 237` continues to mean \"the current turn starts at line 237 of this 252-line transcript\", which is what the UI expects.\n\nA regression test belongs alongside `TestCondenseSession_V2CompactTranscriptStart` in `manual_commit_test.go:4326` — drive a session through finalize and assert that `transcript_lines >= checkpoint_transcript_start` on the resulting `/main` metadata."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2077,"cache_read_input_tokens":95460,"output_tokens":2738,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2077,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2738,"cache_read_input_tokens":95460,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2077},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cajdas